«
@@ ============================================================
@@ VincentyInv — distance and azimuths between two points on the
@@ WGS-84 ellipsoid, the inverse geodetic problem.
@@ T. Vincenty, "Direct and inverse solutions of geodesics on the
@@ ellipsoid with application of nested equations", Survey Review
@@ 23(176), 1975, pp. 88-93.
@@
@@ Input : φ1 λ1 φ2 λ2, latitudes and longitudes, East positive.
@@         Plain numbers are degrees; angles with a unit are accepted.
@@ Output: s α1 α2 — distance in metres, azimuths in degrees from
@@         true North at the departure (α1) and arrival (α2) points.
@@ The iteration converges to 1E-12 radian (about 0.006 mm). It does
@@ not converge for nearly antipodal points: after 200 iterations the
@@ function stops with an error rather than return a wrong value.
@@
@@ The work is done in radians without angle units. The angle mode and
@@ the angle units setting are restored before returning, and before
@@ reporting an error. IFERR is not used: when an error leaves nested
@@ local frames, the locals of its THEN branch no longer designate the
@@ right values.
@@ ============================================================

  @ Angles in radians: plain numbers are degrees
  4 →LIST
  « IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_r CONVERT UVAL ELSE Ⓒπ →Num * 180 / END »
  MAP LIST→ DROP
  Ⓒa♁GPS →Num UVAL Ⓒf♁GPS →Num
  'AngleMode' RCL 'SetAngleUnits' RCL
  RAD NoAngleUnits
  0
  → p1 q1 p2 q2 axa fla amode aunits fail
  «
    'axa*(1-fla)' EVAL 'ATAN((1-fla)*TAN(p1))' EVAL 'ATAN((1-fla)*TAN(p2))' EVAL 'q2-q1' EVAL
    → bxa ur1 ur2 dlon
    «
      ur1 SIN ur1 COS ur2 SIN ur2 COS
      dlon 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      → su1 cu1 su2 cu2 lam lamp ssig csig sgm salf c2a c2m iter
      «
        DO
          lam 'lamp' STO
          '√((cu2*SIN(lam))²+(cu1*su2-su1*cu2*COS(lam))²)' EVAL 'ssig' STO
          'su1*su2+cu1*cu2*COS(lam)' EVAL 'csig' STO
          '(ssig)∠(csig)' EVAL 'sgm' STO
          IF ssig 0 = THEN 0 ELSE 'cu1*cu2*SIN(lam)/ssig' EVAL END 'salf' STO
          '1-salf²' EVAL 'c2a' STO
          IF c2a 0 = THEN 0 ELSE 'csig-2*su1*su2/c2a' EVAL END 'c2m' STO
          'fla/16*c2a*(4+fla*(4-3*c2a))' EVAL
          → cvc
          « 'dlon+(1-cvc)*fla*salf*(sgm+cvc*ssig*(c2m+cvc*csig*(2*c2m²-1)))' EVAL 'lam' STO »
          iter 1 + 'iter' STO
        UNTIL
          'ABS(lam-lamp)' EVAL 1E-12 < iter 200 ≥ OR
        END
        IF 'ABS(lam-lamp)' EVAL 1E-12 ≥ THEN 1 'fail' STO END

        'c2a*(axa²-bxa²)/bxa²' EVAL
        → usq
        «
          '1+usq/16384*(4096+usq*(-768+usq*(320-175*usq)))' EVAL
          'usq/1024*(256+usq*(-128+usq*(74-47*usq)))' EVAL
          → aca bcb
          «
            'bcb*ssig*(c2m+bcb/4*(csig*(2*c2m²-1)-bcb/6*c2m*(4*ssig²-3)*(4*c2m²-3)))' EVAL
            → dsig
            «
              'bxa*aca*(sgm-dsig)' EVAL 1_m *
              '(cu2*SIN(lam))∠(cu1*su2-su1*cu2*COS(lam))' EVAL
              '(cu1*SIN(lam))∠(cu1*su2*COS(lam)-su1*cu2)' EVAL
              2 →LIST
              « 180 * Ⓒπ →Num / 360 MOD 1_° * »
              MAP LIST→ DROP
            »
          »
        »
      »
    »
    amode EVAL IF aunits THEN SetAngleUnits ELSE NoAngleUnits END
    IF fail THEN
      DROP DROP DROP
      "VincentyInv: no convergence (nearly antipodal points)" DOERR
    END
  »
»
